# Wave T49 (Bridgeport kit): mooringpost — an iron mooring bollard with a coil of rope at its base: the harbour's mooring furniture, seated at the canal head (20,1) where the foundry boats tie up on the north reach, and on the east shore (25,10) by the Route 218 landing. Fully opaque: the town grass is baked in (measured #0d8420, tg-canalave's rendered pure flat). (NO-SAME-KIT law; WAVE-T49-BRIDGEPORT-PLAN.md §5.)
